ies not named by this act keep their prior snapshot bytes.","+- 2026-10-09 — refresh under approval. Copied: low-level-requirements.toml (re-attested: LLR-320); test-cases.toml (re-attested: TC-342, TC-343). Registries not named by this act keep their prior snapshot bytes."]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\acts.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":536,"oldLines":3,"newStart":536,"newLines":9,"lines":[" date = \"2026-10-09\""," approved = []"," reattested = [\"LLR-300\", \"LLR-301\", \"LLR-322\", \"TC-339\", \"TC-340\", \"TC-345\"]","+","+[[act]]","+seq = 89","+date = \"2026-10-09\"","+approved = []","+reattested = [\"LLR-320\", \"TC-342\", \"TC-343\"]"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\low-level-requirements.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":3172,"oldLines":7,"newStart":3172,"newLines":7,"lines":[" sr_refs = [\"SR-229\", \"SR-237\"]"," title = \"Coordinator context occupancy, lease, and drain latch\""," module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/coordinator_guard.py;project-trajectory/scripts/integrate.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/shell_line.py\"","-code_symbol = \"GuardConfig/guard_config/Occupancy/read_occupancy/lease_dir/take/release/clear/hand_back/record_event/latch_reading/window_refusal/claim_refusal/on_blackout/launch_reason/model_clis/command_name/command_words/_assigned/window_check/hooks_state/enable_hooks/on_monitored/on_session_start/on_pre_compact/classify_compaction/hook;claim;segments/Unreadable/Word\"","+code_symbol = \"GuardConfig/guard_config/Occupancy/read_occupancy/lease_dir/take/release/clear/hand_back/record_event/latch_reading/window_refusal/claim_refusal/on_blackout/launch_reason/model_clis/command_name/command_words/_assigned/_invoked/window_check/hooks_state/enable_hooks/on_monitored/on_session_start/on_pre_compact/classify_compaction/hook;claim;segments/Unreadable/Word\""," detail = \"guard_config reads the declared coordinator threshold and window: a non-positive, out-of-range or malformed threshold is off and a malformed window reads as the default. read_occupancy reads the newest valid assistant usage after the live transcript branch's latest compaction boundary, never a sidechain record, counting input and cached input; a record whose usage is malformed, partial or zero is skipped, and no valid usage reads as unknown, never zero. A primary-checkout lease names one coordinator session and its transcript. take refuses another holder; release frees the lease and clear unlatches it, each requiring and recording the owner's reason; hand_back accepts only the holder session and a handoff carrying a session prompt, frees the lease, and records the handoff; it refuses another or unnamed caller, whatever handoff it names, while naming the owner's release; it refuses the holder's own pending relaunch request, while a previous holder's request does not block it and is left for session_end's foreign-request refusal; with the guard off it returns before reading or writing. Elapsed time never transfers ownership. on_session_start installs a session as holder, unlatched, only when it presents the successor token the holder's exit wrote into the lease, and restates a latched drain to the holder's own resumed start. Only the holder's own hook payload on the holder's transcript is measured, never a subagent's. latch_reading latches drain when the unrounded reading reaches the threshold and retains it through lower readings, compaction and resume; it ends only through the owner's clear, the owner's release, the holder's hand-back, or a successor take. window_refusal runs before the dial on every claim route, including the dispatcher, naming the UTC end; the dispatcher remains exempt only from the context guard. claim_refusal identifies the claimant by the session id the agent CLI exports to its tool processes (CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID), refuses with no lease held or a claimant that is not the holder, and reads and latches the holder's transcript itself, so a refusal never depends on a hook having run; a claim holding the dispatch lock never calls it. While a window is armed hooks act at every dial and deny the closed list of the main session's Agent call, SendMessage call, Bash/PowerShell model-CLI command word, and a Bash/PowerShell line unreadable only because of an unclosed single quote, unclosed double quote, unclosed POSIX dollar quote, unclosed POSIX backtick substitution, unclosed dollar-parenthesis substitution, or unclosed PowerShell here-string. One quote-aware shell reading per dialect reads quoted assignments and env split strings as the shell does, reads a PowerShell assignment, recognised by an unquoted assignment operator wherever it stands (quotedness is known for every character of a word), whatever its target, as running its right-hand command; a quoted right-hand value and a variable right-hand value stay data, while a chained assignment whose final right-hand side is a command runs that command; treats quoted separators as data, reads substitutions in unquoted here-document and double-quoted PowerShell here-string bodies, and keeps quoted bodies as data; window_check exits nonzero inside it. At every SessionStart inside a window, hooks inject the blackout close-down instruction; each main session's monitored events inject it at that session's first monitored event in the window and every twentieth thereafter, counted per session per window: bring each open lane to its pause point, using a wrap-up adjudication for an active claim where needed; write the handoff naming each lane and its next obligation; request no relaunch; and end the session. Hook responses inject the latch instruction once and bounded reminders thereafter. PreCompact records trigger, occupancy and latch/request state; classify_compaction reports missed-threshold, manual and during-drain cases.\""," rationale = \"The context reading and lease are one admission fact: without one holder and a latched record, a tool-event observation can be missed and a later claim can start new work after the coordinator should be closing out.\""," test_refs = \"TC-315;TC-316;TC-317\""]},{"oldStart":3402,"oldLines":7,"newStart":3402,"newLines":7,"lines":[" title = \"Dev-setup readiness operation for a bare run\""," module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/dev-setup.template.sh;project-trajectory/scripts/dev-setup.template.ps1;project-trajectory/scripts/dev-setup.template.cmd;project-trajectory/scripts/dev-setup.template.command\""," code_symbol = \"detect_runtime/interactive/maybe_install;FindPython/Interactive/MaybeInstall\"","-detail = \"The --for-run/-ForRun operation reports workstation readiness first, then offers each missing setup item only at an interactive terminal; without one it offers nothing and does not consume menu input. Its runtime is the interpreter the launcher hands it, never one it searches for: it exits 0 when that interpreter satisfies the runtime floor and otherwise, including when none is handed, exits 1 with the step to take. The standalone --check/-Check operation reports only, performs no offer or write, and exits 0.\"","+detail = \"The --for-run/-ForRun operation reports workstation readiness first, querying a workstation tool only once it is found present and reporting an absent one as missing, so an absent tool never ends the report before its runtime result; it then offers each missing setup item only at an interactive terminal, and without one it offers nothing and does not consume menu input. Its runtime is the interpreter the launcher hands it, never one it searches for: it exits 0 when that interpreter satisfies the runtime floor and otherwise, including when none is handed, exits 1 with the step to take. The standalone --check/-Check operation reports only, performs no offer or write, and exits 0.\""," rationale = \"A menu can be useful only after its runtime is usable, but the readiness step must not turn a piped or automated launch into an unattended installer.\""," test_refs = \"TC-343\""," status = \"Approved\""]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":3477,"oldLines":22,"newStart":3477,"newLines":22,"lines":[" [test.TC-342]"," verifies = [\"SR-032\", \"SR-046\", \"IF-157\", \"IF-158\", \"IF-292\", \"LLR-047\", \"IF-293\"]"," level = \"Integration\"","-method = \"Run bare, direct and list launchers against a scaffold and the repository with varied readiness results, observing the interpreter handed to the readiness step and the one the menu runs on, and with only sub-floor interpreters first on PATH; compare each launcher's candidate list with its dev-setup's runtime search.\"","+method = \"Run bare, direct and list launchers against a scaffold and the repository with varied readiness results, observing the interpreter handed to the readiness step and the one the menu runs on, and with only sub-floor interpreters first on PATH; compare each launcher's candidate list with its dev-setup's runtime search. Run a bare Windows launcher on a scaffold and on the repository with a working runtime and no Git on PATH.\""," tier = \"Full\"","-expected = \"A bare run checks once before its menu, handing the check the interpreter the menu then runs on, and stops on a missing runtime; direct and list forms do not check or pause; with no Python 3.11+ interpreter no form starts the menu; each launcher searches the same interpreters, in the same order, as its dev-setup.\"","+expected = \"A bare run checks once before its menu, handing the check the interpreter the menu then runs on, and stops on a missing runtime; direct and list forms do not check or pause; with no Python 3.11+ interpreter no form starts the menu; each launcher searches the same interpreters, in the same order, as its dev-setup; without Git a bare run still reaches its menu.\""," automated = \"Yes\"","-evidence = \"tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_bare_run_calls_the_check_once_from_the_root_before_the_menu; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_bare_run_stops_with_the_step_when_the_runtime_stays_missing; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_direct_and_list_forms_never_call_the_check; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_bare_run_cmd_calls_the_check_once_from_the_root_before_the_menu; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_direct_and_list_forms_of_run_cmd_never_check_or_pause; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_check_for_run_offers_nothing_without_a_terminal; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_piped_menu_input_survives_the_check; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_this_repos_run_shows_its_menu_after_the_check; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_bare_run_hands_the_check_the_interpreter_its_menu_runs_on; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_no_form_of_run_starts_the_menu_below_the_floor; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_each_run_launcher_searches_what_its_dev_setup_searches\"","+evidence = \"tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_bare_run_calls_the_check_once_from_the_root_before_the_menu; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_bare_run_stops_with_the_step_when_the_runtime_stays_missing; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_direct_and_list_forms_never_call_the_check; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_bare_run_cmd_calls_the_check_once_from_the_root_before_the_menu; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_direct_and_list_forms_of_run_cmd_never_check_or_pause; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_check_for_run_offers_nothing_without_a_terminal; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_piped_menu_input_survives_the_check; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_this_repos_run_shows_its_menu_after_the_check; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_bare_run_hands_the_check_the_interpreter_its_menu_runs_on; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_no_form_of_run_starts_the_menu_below_the_floor; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_each_run_launcher_searches_what_its_dev_setup_searches; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_without_git_the_check_reports_it_missing_and_the_run_reaches_its_menu; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_without_git_this_repos_check_and_run_still_work\""," status = \"Approved\""," phase = 6"," "," [test.TC-343]"," verifies = [\"SR-032\", \"LLR-320\"]"," level = \"Integration\"","-method = \"Run the readiness operation with interactive and non-interactive input, a missing runtime, and piped menu input; also run the standalone check. At a terminal, drive each missing-item offer through consent; drive standalone check at a terminal. Run the readiness operation with and without a handed interpreter while a Python 3.11+ interpreter is on PATH.\"","+method = \"Run the readiness operation with interactive and non-interactive input, a missing runtime, and piped menu input; also run the standalone check. At a terminal, drive each missing-item offer through consent; drive standalone check at a terminal. Run the readiness operation with and without a handed interpreter while a Python 3.11+ interpreter is on PATH. Run it, and the standalone check, with a working runtime and no Git on PATH.\""," tier = \"Full\"","-expected = \"The operation reports before offering, offers nothing without a terminal, preserves piped menu input, and exits with guidance when the runtime remains missing; standalone check is read-only and exits 0. At a terminal each missing item is offered consent-first, while standalone check offers and writes nothing. Without a handed interpreter it reports the runtime missing and exits 1 although a Python 3.11+ interpreter is on PATH; with one that satisfies the floor it exits 0.\"","+expected = \"The operation reports before offering, offers nothing without a terminal, preserves piped menu input, and exits with guidance when the runtime remains missing; standalone check is read-only and exits 0. At a terminal each missing item is offered consent-first, while standalone check offers and writes nothing. Without a handed interpreter it reports the runtime missing and exits 1 although a Python 3.11+ interpreter is on PATH; with one that satisfies the floor it exits 0. Without Git, the operation reports git missing and still exits 0 with a runtime, and the standalone check exits 0.\""," automated = \"Yes\"","-evidence = \"tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_check_for_run_offers_nothing_without_a_terminal; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_piped_menu_input_survives_the_check; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_bare_run_cmd_stops_with_the_step_when_the_runtime_stays_missing; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_at_a_terminal_each_missing_item_is_offered_consent_first; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_standalone_check_at_a_terminal_offers_and_writes_nothing; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_check_for_run_checks_only_the_interpreter_it_is_handed\"","+evidence = \"tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_check_for_run_offers_nothing_without_a_terminal; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_piped_menu_input_survives_the_check; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_bare_run_cmd_stops_with_the_step_when_the_runtime_stays_missing; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_at_a_terminal_each_missing_item_is_offered_consent_first; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_standalone_check_at_a_terminal_offers_and_writes_nothing; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_check_for_run_checks_only_the_interpreter_it_is_handed; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_without_git_the_check_reports_it_missing_and_the_run_reaches_its_menu\""," status = \"Approved\""," phase = 6"," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\README.md","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\acts.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\low-level-requirements.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml"]}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfsaiK8xPy66dBpUQKhd3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three amended rows change meaning, and I blessed and re-attested each one. The verdict is `f6ee7daf` and the re-attestation is `1403811a`'s successor, `1fa66e24`. Both end with `WI: WI-834` and passed the commit hooks; the snapshot copied the LLR and TC registries without refusal.\n\n**amendment: `VERDICT: MEANING rows=3`.** All three add the same obligation: a workstation without Git still gets its full readiness report and reaches the menu.\n- **LLR-320:** dev-setup must query a tool only once it is found present, so a missing tool never ends the report before the runtime result. That is a new robustness rule.\n- **TC-342 and TC-343:** each adds a Git-less test case: a bare run still reaches the menu, the check reports Git missing and still exits 0, and the standalone check exits 0.\n\n**What I checked:**\n- The fix itself was PowerShell-specific. Under `ErrorActionPreference = \"Stop\"`, calling the missing `git` threw before the runtime result. Both the kit's template and this repo's `scripts/dev-setup.ps1` now check `Have \"git\"` first.\n- The two new Git-less tests ran on this Windows host and passed. The wider suites gave `151 passed, 5 skipped`, with the same known skips as before.\n- No test covers the POSIX path, so I ran the POSIX template myself with no `git` on PATH. Both `--check` and `--for-run` reported Git missing, finished the report and exited 0.\n\nOne observation, not a return: the POSIX template still runs `git config` without first checking that Git exists. It meets LLR-320's outcome only because shell rules let that failure pass harmlessly, not through the presence check the row describes. A later pass could add the same guard to the POSIX script, or reword the row to state just the outcome.\n\nMy probe script is in the session scratchpad. The `.requested` marker is left untracked for the coordinator."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":688,"cache_read_input_tokens":514864,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":688},"output_tokens":645,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8d8d1fbc-6a42-4a02-9ec0-8f8d2b61c24c","uuid":"df840ccb-1082-427a-a9c4-0ecc160ec2b4","timestamp":"2026-10-10T00:07:19.314Z","request_id":"req_011CfsaiJiQzi6G2hoRkEZcn"}
